=== REASONING ===

Why NARRATIVE render contract, not proposal/suggestion:
  The /exports page is a list view of past export jobs (table + bulk-delete + download). It is NOT an export-creation form. There is no in-flight typed draft for an "Apply to form" affordance to copy values into. The user's path to act on a redaction recommendation is to navigate elsewhere (Settings or a future export-builder flow) and toggle the matching options. Ergo NARRATIVE is the only honest render contract for this slice; the typed validation envelope from validate_export_redaction_plan stays inside the dispatcher loop and surfaces to the user as the narrator's prose.

Why STATIC catalog, not per-row PII scan:
  ADR-015 §I3 (baseline intact) + §I4 (zero unintended egress) forbid us from inspecting actual export-row content via the AI path. A per-row scan would (a) mean the LLM saw raw user-PII row-by-row, breaking I4, and (b) duplicate the deterministic export pipeline, breaking I3. The catalog is keyed by export_type and lists the PII classes the canonical export pipeline is known to emit for that type — every recommendation is structurally derivable from the export shape, never from the user's specific data. The strategy's system prompt + the goldens' answer_must_contain pin "catalog-based" + "not a per-row PII scan" as load-bearing honesty disclosures so a future regression that secretly added a per-row scan would fail eval immediately.

Why two tools (draft + validate), not one:
  This mirrors slice 0051's draft/validate split (and other M-tier slices' draft/validate splits). draft_export_redaction_plan returns the catalog envelope verbatim; validate_export_redaction_plan returns ok=true/false plus a typed errors[] list when the LLM's candidate plan misses a highly_recommended class or uses an unrecognized mode. The system prompt makes refusal MANDATORY when ok=false; this is the I3 + I8 propose-only contract enforced inside the dispatcher loop, before any narrative reaches the user.

Why per-request scope binding via WithScopedSharedExportRedactionWindow:
  The handler installs a context value naming the in-scope export_type before the dispatcher fires. Each tool's Validate refuses any export_type that does not match the scope. This defends against prompt-injection — a malicious release-note string or user-message fragment that tries to make the LLM call draft_export_redaction_plan with a different export_type cannot exfiltrate the catalog row for that other type, because the tool refuses the call before the registry resolves it. Same hygiene that slice 0051 (vehicle-id-scoped) and 0049 (TCO-scope-bound) already applied.

Why PolicyAlertBuilder, not PolicyDeny / PolicyNumeric:
  PolicyAlertBuilder is the broadest existing policy that allows the model's output to mention class names ("email", "phone", "license_plate") which the catalog's recommendations literally name. PolicyDeny would redact the recommendations to opacity; PolicyNumeric is for numeric-only outputs. The catalog itself is PII-free by construction (it lists CLASSES of PII, not actual PII values), so the policy is defence-in-depth rather than load-bearing here.

Why the SPA component renders through AIFeatureCard with `inputSlot`:
  The HX addendum mandates the shared scaffold. The export_type Select is a form input, so it goes in `inputSlot` (the AIFeatureCard auto-sets buttonPlacement='below' when an inputSlot is present, which gives the button room to live below the Select trigger). The verb "Suggest redactions" is passed as `buttonLabel` per HX rule 2 — never "Ask Helix" — so the accessible name composes as "Ask Helix · Suggest redactions" and the on-mode wiring test's unanchored regex `/Suggest redactions/i` matches. This satisfies both W1 (wired-or-absent + computed disabled) and HX (shared scaffold + branded copy + brand glyph + unanchored selectors) without bespoke layout.

Why useAiStream wired against /ai/exports/redaction/draft:
  The hook prepends `${getApiBase()}/api/v1`, so the SPA `url='/ai/exports/redaction/draft'` produces a final POST to `/api/v1/ai/exports/redaction/draft` — this is the EXACT path registered in the registry's RouteSet.Backend and mounted by mountAIRoutes via g.Wrap("pii-redaction-shared-exports", …). The on-mode wiring test asserts the literal final URL so a typo here is caught by Vitest before it ever reaches production.

